course: dictionary
lesson: 11575
title: Words that mean wiped out
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «Annihilated» is a strong word. It is the past form of «annihilate», and it means destroyed completely, with nothing left. «The storm annihilated the sandcastles on the beach.» Nothing is left of the sandcastles, not even a small wall.
explain: The word also appears in sport. «Our team was annihilated 9-0 in the final.» The other team did not just win, they beat us very badly. You can check the meaning by asking: what word would fit here? Destroyed or beaten badly both fit, so the meaning is strong and complete.
explain: Notice the clues around the word. The storm, the sandcastles and the word «completely» all point to total destruction. When you meet a new word, read the words around it first, then test your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
fact: «Annihilated» comes from «annihilate», which means destroy completely.
fact: «Annihilated» means wiped out, with nothing left behind.
fact: In sport, «annihilated» means beaten very badly in a game or contest.
fact: In science, matter and antimatter annihilate each other when they meet, so both are destroyed.
fact: «Completely annihilated» is a phrase that makes the destruction even stronger.
exercise: «The storm annihilated the sandcastles on the beach.» What does annihilated mean here? | Washed clean | *Destroyed completely | Painted in bright colours | Built up carefully
exercise: «Our team was annihilated 9-0 in the final.» What does annihilated suggest? | *We lost very badly | The match was a draw | We won by one point | We played for fun with no score
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to annihilated? | Sang | Mended | *Wiped out | Tidied
test: When matter and antimatter meet in science, what happens to them? | *They are destroyed completely | They change colour | They fall asleep | They grow larger
test: Why would a sports writer say «the visitors were annihilated»? | The visitors were given a prize | The visitors won the trophy easily | The visitors had a picnic on the pitch | *The visitors lost very badly
exam: «The old city was annihilated in the war.» What does annihilated mean here? | *Destroyed completely | Built up with care | Painted a light colour | Covered in snow
